      "writtenOn": "2023-07-28T03:00:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The API classes are being added to an S+ bootclasspath jar, so we need to decide what to do in that case\nMaybe each method would throw an UnsupportedOperationException if called on U-, before trying to call the service implementations ?\n\nAt build time this jar is getting included into the service-connectivity jar, which is really loaded by devices in the field on S+, so at build time it really needs to be 31+; although at runtime the classes would only be loaded on V+. I don\u0027t think the build system supports this use-case: \"this library is built into a 31+ jar, but its users won\u0027t try to load the classes before V+\". You might have to annotate each class with @RequiresApi(V) at the moment.",
      "parentUuid": "b1585e55_71137da8",
